      "writtenOn": "2021-07-16T08:40:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Fair enough.\n\nI used \"this\" as the lock object (in spite of go/synchronized-this-considered-harmful because this lock already escapes anyway) to avoid the overhead of creating a new object just for this. Note that there are already some instances of synchronized (this) so it increases a little bit the lock contention, but it looks rarely used and I don\u0027t think it would be significant at all.\nAlso I only locked accesses to mInitialApplication in this use case ; I didn\u0027t want to increase lock contention everywhere it\u0027s accessed. That means I made the boolean @GuardedBy, but not mInitialApplication because most of the time it\u0027s not accessed locked and doesn\u0027t need to be.\n\nLet me know if you\u0027d prefer a separate object for this lock.",
      "parentUuid": "6ef19cfe_7647a4b2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1134,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 1134,
        "endChar": 49
