      "writtenOn": "2021-07-16T09:15:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah this should be fine to me. Understood that using \u0027this\u0027 would potentially increase the possibility of lock contentions (thus the monitor object \u0027this\u0027 could become a fat lock, so each synchronized(this) won\u0027t be cheap anymore) - yet I\u0027m feeling that using a different lock might be overkilling.\n\nMaybe another idea here is, now sure if it would be okay or not: if all the updateHttpProxy() does is only to post a runnable to the main handler thread, something like this:\n\npublic void updateHttpProxy() {\n   mH.post(() -\u003e {\n       final Application app \u003d getApplication();\n       if (app \u003d\u003d null) {\n           mUpdateHttpProxyOnBind \u003d true;\n           return;\n       }\n       ActivityThread.updateHttpProxy(app);\n   });\n}\n\nmeanwhile, in the handleBindApplication():\n\nprivate void handleBindApplication(AppBindData data) {\n    ...\n    if (mUpdateHttpProxyOnBind) {\n       ActivityThread.updateHttpProxy(app);\n    }\n    ...\n}\n\nBy doing this, there is no lock needed because they\u0027re all in the main thread, the only drawback here is that, the http proxy update would take effect a little bit late than before.",
      "parentUuid": "65ac718c_766ddd7d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1134,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 1134,
        "endChar": 49
