      "writtenOn": "2021-07-19T03:05:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure the delay is acceptable in practice. Apps are supposed to listen to PROXY_CHANGE_ACTION to know when to read the proxy, and reading from the system properties (while not the documented way) is a common way of doing this.\n\nIf it becomes possible that the app processes the (sticky) broadcast before the system properties are set, then we\u0027re going to break apps. I get that it is very unlikely if it\u0027s a handler loop racing against a broadcast receiver, but the bug would also be very difficult to diagnose.",
      "parentUuid": "e802d768_ecce2c48",
